VOTING OPTIONS AND DETAILS INSIDE! 

Vote in-person at a Vote Center Oct. 24 - Nov. 3, 2026 Consider voting at home – your ballot will arrive soon through the mail Multiple options for returning your ballot – via secure drop box or by mail 

> VOTE CENTER HOURS HAVE CHANGED! DETAILS INSIDE

CALIFORNIA GENERAL ELECTION 

General Election Tuesday, November 3, 2026 

Official Voter Information Guide Don’t Delay, Vote Today! Return your ballot as soon as you receive it. Vote-by-mail early voting period opens October 5, 2026. Polls are open from 7:00 a.m. to 8:00 p.m. on November 3, 2026, Election Day! 

Every registered voter in California will receive a ballot by mail. Ballots are mailed on or before October 5. Ballots can be voted and returned as soon as they are received. Ballot drop boxes open October 6. In-person voting options will be available in all counties. 

